From 5f12c140e2ee8fbd183edd65795c493c191ed60b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:57:10 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 071/230] Debug Telegram auth + clean up dead ad code
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Telegram auth bug (initData not reaching the server):
- src/lib/auth.ts: telegramInitData() now logs { hasWebApp, sdkInitData, captured }
  so the browser console shows exactly what each source is returning.
- src/lib/telegramUrl.ts: applyTelegramUrlNormalization() now logs
  { sdkInitData, captured, changed, newUrl } and its load-bearing ordering
  (must run before auth) is stated in the doc comment. main.tsx already mounts
  on tg-sdk-settled and calls this first, so the URL is cleaned and the init
  data is captured before AuthProvider reads it.
- src/hooks/useAuth.tsx: enterApp now warns "[auth] enterApp called with no
  initData" when initData is null, and logs the first 40 chars of the initData
  string right before api.guest(getDeviceId(), initData).

Dead ad code cleanup:
- src/lib/ads.ts deleted — no importers remain (AdBanner.tsx already deleted).
- vite.config.ts: __ADS_ENABLED__ inlined from _env.ADS_ENABLED only; the
  unused env var is prefixed with _ so the linter allows it.
- src/vite-env.d.ts: removed the now-unused __ADS_ENABLED__ declare and the
  VITE_ADS_ENABLED ImportMetaEnv member.

Gates: typecheck, lint, format, tests, build.
